{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 6, :comments ["<b>השותים</b> — 'wine' is the construct noun and it is in construct state, but the word in construct is not mentioned, only 'in basins of silver or gold.' R. Marinus said: the bet is superfluous, like לכו לחמו בלחמי ושתו ביין מסכתי (Isaiah 21:5)." "<b>על שבר יוסף</b> — the kingdom of Jeroboam."], :book :amos, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 6, :notes {0 "The word הנסמך ('the word in construct') seems to refer to the implied noun paired with 'במזרקי'; the syntax of this sentence is compressed and its exact referent is uncertain."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Amos -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/amos"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:18:19.884517825Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}